Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Play animated GIF, APNG and WebP images in the iOS reader

Decoders keep producing one still frame (all the Mac and every still path
see) and attach an AnimatedImageSource: frame count, delays (10 ms or less
plays as 100 ms, as in browsers) and loop count. AnimatedImageView streams
frames, decoding the next one on a background queue at its on-screen size
and keeping about two in memory: the README demo GIF is 216 MB if decoded
up front. It runs only in a window, on screen, with the app active and
Reduce Motion off.

Block and inline images are played by a live view the reader places over
the picture's space (ImageFragment's rect; frameForTextAttachment inline).
NSTextAttachmentViewProvider was tried first; its views were never hosted
by this reader's custom layout fragments.

Tests: AnimatedImageTests and a RemoteImageLoader GIF test. check-ios 420
tests; Mac check.sh unchanged at 1387.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
